body
  div id=root
    div id=app
      div id=top-chrome
        div id=logo-etc
          div id=logoa href=.img src=data:imagepng;base64,
                alt=Phytozome: the plant genomics resourceadiv
        div
        div id=menu-controls
          div class=pz-horizontal-menu
            ul class=pz-top-level-menu
              lia href=https:jgi.doe.govJGI Homeali
              lia href=https:data.jgi.doe.govrefine-downloadphytozomeJGI Data Portalali
              lia href=https:jgi.doe.govuser-programspmo-overviewpolicies#jgi-data-policyJGI Data Policyali              
            ul
          div
        div
      div
      main id=content
        div class=home-body
          div class=intro-text
            section class=announcement
              p style=text-align: left; font-size: 0.8em; line-height: 1.5;Since 7:45 AM Pacific on Monday, November 9, 2026, Phytozome’s services have been impacted by unexpected maintenance on our infrastructure. We regret the inconvenience this creates and are working with teams at a href=https:www.lbl.govLBLa to resolve the issue. We do not yet have an estimate for when services will be back online. Thank you for your patience. We will remove this message as soon as Phytozome is available again.p
            section
            section
              pPhytozome, the Plant Comparative Genomics portal of the Department of Energys Joint Genome Institute, provides JGI users and the broader plant science community a hub for accessing, visualizing and analyzing JGI-sequenced plant genomes, as well as selected genomes and datasets that have been sequenced elsewhere. By integrating this large collection of plant genomes into a single resource and performing comprehensive and uniform annotation and analyses, Phytozome facilitates accurate and insightful comparative genomics studies.p
              pAll gene sets in Phytozome have been annotated with KOG, KEGG, ENZYME, Pathway and the InterPro family of protein analysis tools. Inparanoid-DIAMOND pairwise orthology and paralogy groups have been calculated across all Phytozome proteomes. Families of related genes representing the modern descendants of putative ancestral genes are constructed at key phylogenetic nodes. These families provide additional insight into clade-specific orthologyparalogy relationships as well as clade-specific novelties and expansions. Search and visualization tools let users quickly find and analyze genes or genomic regions of interest. Query-based data access is provided by Phytozomes PhytoMine and BioMart instances, while bulk data sets can be accessed via the JGIs Genome Portal. JBrowse genome browsers are available for all genomes.p
              pem class=boldCiting Phytozome:em David M. Goodstein, Shengqiang Shu, Russell Howson, Rochak Neupane, Richard D. Hayes, Joni Fazo, Therese Mitros, William Dirks, Uffe Hellsten, Nicholas Putnam, and Daniel S. Rokhsar, em class=boldPhytozome: a comparative platform for green plant genomicsem, a href=http:nar.oxfordjournals.orgcontent40D1D1178Nucleic Acids Res. 2012 40 (D1): D1178-D1186ap
            section
          div
        div
      main
      div id=footer
        ul id=footer-links
          lia href=cdn-cgilemail-protection#57273f2e23382d383a32173d303e7a27243179382530Contactali
          lia href=http:jgi.doe.govdisclaimerDisclaimerali
          lia href=http:jgi.doe.govaccessibility-section-508-statementAccessibility  Section 508 Statementali
          li©2016-2025 The Regents of the University of Californiali
        ul
        div id=doe-office-of-science
          a href=http:science.energy.gov
            img src=data:imagepng;base64, 
          a
      div
    div
  div
